course: dictionary
lesson: 14195
title: Words that push you forward
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word «motivating» comes from the verb «motivate», which means to make someone want to do something or try hard. When something is motivating, it gives you that push. «Stars on the wall are motivating for many children.» The stars make the children want to try.
explain: «Motivating» can also describe something that gives you energy and the wish to keep going. «The coach's short talk was really motivating, and we ran faster in the last lap.» Words like this often tell you why someone acted.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Ask yourself: what made someone want to try harder? In «The big goal on the wall was motivating for the whole team», the goal is the reason the team worked hard. Then swap in a simpler idea, such as "a thing that makes you want to try", and check the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Motivate is a verb: to make someone want to do something or try hard.
fact: «Motivating» can describe a thing that gives you energy and the wish to keep going.
fact: «Motivating» can also mean being the reason behind something, as in «the motivating idea».
fact: Useful phrases: «motivating factor», «find it motivating», «motivating yourself».
exercise: «The reading badge was motivating, so Priya read every night.» What does motivating mean here? | Making her feel sleepy | Making the badge heavy | *Making her want to read and try hard | Making the reading shorter
exercise: Which verb is motivating made from? | Motion | *Motivate | Mention | Moan
exercise: «The cheering crowd was motivating for the runners.» What does this sentence tell you? | The crowd was asleep | The crowd went home early | The runners were lost | *The crowd made the runners want to keep going
test: «Our class plan with stars on the wall is motivating.» What does motivating most likely mean in this sentence? | Too big to see | Very cold | *Making us want to try hard | Boring and dull
test: Mia says, "I find it motivating when Dad claps for me." What does this mean? | The claps mean it is time for bed | She finds the claps hard to hear | She finds the claps funny | *The claps make her want to keep trying
exam: «The coach said the team's effort was motivating, and the motivating idea was to win together.» What does motivating mean in the second part? | Very quiet | Written down | Hard to play | *The reason that makes the team act
